  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Allow a fourth tracker to track an arbitrary object that is either part of the user's avatar heirachy, or a vrchat world object.\n\nHere's a possible way to implement it:\n\nAvatar object.\nWithin the user's avatar heirachy, a single mesh object, named object_track*. This object is bound to the fourth non-body tracker at its origin and aligns its local coordinates to the trackers.\noptional: A menu toggle to disable sync of this, so it's local only if so desired.\nIf no fourth tracker is found, this object is disabled.\n\nWorld object.\nVery similar to avatar object, but a regular pickup with a different coloured highlight (indicating it can be bound to your fourth tracker). To bind: Pick up, the fourth tracker now shows like in full-body calibration. Align the world object, and the tracker, 'use' the object. It is now bound to the tracker.\n\nOptions for world object:\nSingle or Multi-use.\nSingle is a unique object that can only be used one user at a time.\nMulti-use allows any number of users to bind this object to their object tracker, with the original interactable staying in place.\n\n* - just an example name, but you get the idea.\n\nBonus round: Have a small community competition to model a variety of cups and bottles and such to be included in the SDK as tracked object prefabs.",
